---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const features=[
 {title:'ConsDRED',meta:'IEEE TASE 2025 · IROS 2025 presentation',summary:'Constrained distributional reinforcement learning for trustworthy quadrotor tracking control.',image:'/research/consdred-demo-still.jpg',alt:'Quadrotor demonstration still',links:[['Paper','https://doi.org/10.1109/TASE.2024.3432405'],['Project','https://alex-yanranwang.github.io/ConsDRED-SMPC.html'],['Overview','/research/consdred/']]},
 {title:'AWaVO',meta:'ICML 2024',summary:'Probabilistic constrained reinforcement learning with formal interpretability.',image:'/research/awavo-figure-1.png',alt:'Figure 1 from AWaVO: graphical model for constrained RL',links:[['Paper','https://proceedings.mlr.press/v235/wang24bf.html'],['Project','https://alex-yanranwang.github.io/AWaVO.html']]},
 {title:'Functional interpretability',meta:'ICML 2025',summary:'Inducing, detecting and characterising neural modules in reinforcement learning.',image:'/research/icml-modularity.png',alt:'Neural modularity research figure',links:[['Paper','https://proceedings.mlr.press/v267/soligo25a.html'],['Project','https://sites.google.com/view/mod-xrl/home'],['Code','https://github.com/annasoligo/BIXRL']]},
 {title:'MM-Open5x',meta:'IEEE AMES 2026',summary:'Multi-material multi-axis additive manufacturing for practical conformal electronics.',image:'/research/mm-open5x-original.png',alt:'MM-Open5x paper illustration',links:[['Code','https://github.com/BigKoala33/MM-Open5x'],['Related Open5x work','/research/open5x/']]},
];
---
<Base title="Research">
<main class="wrap feature-index">
 <div class="feature-index-intro"><span>RESEARCH / SYSAL</span><h1>Research</h1><p>SysAL develops algorithms, systems and tools for the physical world. Our work spans learning and control, mission-level planning, learning for intelligent communications, 3D-printed electronics, and privacy-preserving sensing.</p></div>
 <section class="strand-strand" aria-labelledby="autonomy-heading"><div class="strand-strand-intro"><span>01 / RESEARCH AREA</span><h2 id="autonomy-heading">Learning, control and trustworthy autonomy</h2><p>We study how autonomous systems learn, make decisions and operate reliably under uncertainty, combining reinforcement learning, predictive control and interpretability.</p></div><div class="feature-index-list">{features.slice(0,3).map(p=><article class="feature-index-entry"><div class="feature-index-image"><img src={p.image} alt={p.alt} loading="lazy"/></div><div><span class="feature-item-index">{p.meta}</span><h3>{p.title}</h3><p>{p.summary}</p><div class="feature-inline-links">{p.links.map(l=><a href={l[1]}>{l[0]} ↗</a>)}</div></div></article>)}</div><div class="join-autonomy-extras">
  <article class="planning-paper"><span class="feature-item-index">IEEE INTERNET OF THINGS JOURNAL · 2025</span><h3>Is That Rain?</h3><p>Rain effects on visual odometry for autonomous aerial vehicles, with efficient edge-based rain classification.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/JIOT.2025.3547425">Paper ↗</a><a href="https://ieee-dataport.org/documents/adverse-rainy-conditions-autonomous-uavs">Dataset ↗</a></div></article>
  <article class="planning-paper"><span class="feature-item-index">CoRL · 2023</span><h3>QuaDUE-CCM</h3><p>Interpretable distributional reinforcement learning using uncertain contraction metrics for precise quadrotor trajectory tracking.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v205/wang23d.html">Paper ↗</a></div></article>
</div></section>
 <section class="strand-strand" aria-labelledby="planning-heading"><div class="strand-strand-intro"><span>02 / RESEARCH AREA</span><h2 id="planning-heading">Planning and decision-making under uncertainty</h2><p>Autonomous systems must decide not only how to act, but what to do next. We develop methods for mission-level planning, routing and resource allocation when costs, opportunities and operating conditions are uncertain or change over time.</p><p>Our work combines combinatorial optimisation, probabilistic modelling and adaptive replanning, connecting high-level mission decisions to the constraints of physical systems.</p></div>
 <div class="planning-paper-list">
  <article class="planning-paper"><span class="feature-item-index">EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF OPERATIONAL RESEARCH · 2024</span><h3>Close-enough orienteering</h3><p>CRaSZe-AntS optimises routes and service locations across overlapping target regions, accounting for resource budgets and non-uniform service costs.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejor.2024.05.032">Paper ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/sysal-bruce-publication/CRaSZe-AntS">Code ↗</a></div></article>
  <article class="planning-paper"><span class="feature-item-index">IEEE INTERNET OF THINGS JOURNAL · 2025</span><h3>ADAPT: adaptive probabilistic planning</h3><p>Combining offline planning, Bayesian energy-cost estimation and online replanning for UAV missions servicing wireless rechargeable sensor networks under uncertain conditions.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/JIOT.2025.3525985">Paper ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/sysal-bruce-publication/Uncertain-Dynamic-OP">Code ↗</a></div></article>
 </div></section>
 <section class="strand-strand" aria-labelledby="communications-heading"><div class="strand-strand-intro"><span>03 / RESEARCH AREA</span><h2 id="communications-heading">Learning for intelligent communications</h2><p>We investigate how learning-based methods can improve the performance, adaptability and trustworthiness of wireless communication systems. Our work combines reinforcement learning, multi-agent decision-making and network optimisation to address mobility, resource allocation, energy efficiency and service quality.</p><p>A particular focus is aerial communications, where platform trajectories and wireless resources must be optimised together. We also examine how explainable and causal learning can help people understand and trust AI-driven networks.</p></div>
 <div class="communications-paper-list">
  <article class="planning-paper"><span class="feature-item-index">IEEE TMLCN · 2024</span><h3>Multi-agent learning for aerial networks</h3><p>Shared deep Q-learning with action masking coordinates multiple UAVs, their three-dimensional trajectories and NOMA power allocation as mobile user groups change.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TMLCN.2024.3521876">Paper ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/smrizvi1/Multi-Agent-RL-with-Invalid-action-Masking">Code ↗</a></div></article>
  <article class="planning-paper"><span class="feature-item-index">AD HOC NETWORKS · 2026</span><h3>Airborne STAR-RIS communications</h3><p>Dual-actor reinforcement learning jointly optimises UAV movement, beamforming and coupled reconfigurable-surface coefficients, balancing throughput, energy and fairness in simulation.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.adhoc.2026.104468">Paper ↗</a></div></article>
  <article class="planning-paper"><span class="feature-item-index">IEEE OJ-COMS · 2025</span><h3>Explainable learning for 6G</h3><p>A review of stakeholder-specific explanations, reinforcement learning and causal understanding for trustworthy AI-enabled communications, including network slicing and UAV use cases.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/OJCOMS.2025.3563415">Paper ↗</a></div></article>
 </div></section>
 <section class="strand-strand" aria-labelledby="fabrication-heading"><div class="strand-strand-intro"><span>04 / RESEARCH AREA</span><h2 id="fabrication-heading">3D-printed electronics and digital fabrication</h2><p>We develop accessible fabrication tools and methods for integrating electronics into three-dimensional forms, from thermoformed circuits to five-axis and multi-material printing.</p></div>
<div class="fabrication-fabrication-list">
  <article class="fabrication-fabrication-entry"><img src="/research/open5x-chi-p4-fig2.png" alt="Open5x printer producing support-free turbine and fan shapes" loading="lazy"/><div><h3>Open5x / MM-Open5x</h3><p>Five-axis desktop printing, conformal toolpaths and multi-material electronics.</p><div class="fabrication-entry-links"><a href="/research/open5x/">Explore the project ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/BigKoala33/MM-Open5x">MM-Open5x code ↗</a></div><p class="bibliography-paper-note">MM-Open5x: Practical Conformal Electronics via Multi-Material Multi-Axis Additive Manufacturing · IEEE AMES 2026 · To appear.</p></div></article>
  <article class="fabrication-fabrication-entry"><img src="/research/curved-traces-am2023.png" alt="Open5x slicing visualisation and fabrication of conductive traces on a curved substrate, from Additive Manufacturing 2023" loading="lazy"/><div><h3>Curved electrical traces</h3><p>Five-axis, multi-material printing deposits conductive traces along curved surfaces, improving electrical performance compared with planar deposition.</p><div class="fabrication-entry-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.addma.2023.103546">Paper ↗</a></div></div></article>
  <article class="fabrication-fabrication-entry"><img src="/research/conformal-antennas-ames2025.png" alt="Rendered conformal patch and double-curvature ultra-wideband antenna designs" loading="lazy"/><div><h3>Conformal antennas</h3><p>Desktop five-axis multi-material fabrication of S-band patch and ultra-wideband antennas, with measured performance against planar-printed counterparts.</p><div class="fabrication-entry-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/AMES64994.2025.11184376">Paper ↗</a></div></div></article>
  <article class="fabrication-fabrication-entry"><img src="/research/conformal-power-spacechi2025.png" alt="Conformal voltage regulator during printing, after electroplating and after component assembly" loading="lazy"/><div><h3>Conformal power electronics</h3><p>Multi-layer surface-mounted circuitry and an assembled switching regulator printed on a curved substrate, explored for resilient space systems.</p><div class="fabrication-entry-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.4230/OASIcs.SpaceCHI.2025.19">Paper ↗</a></div></div></article>
  <article class="fabrication-fabrication-entry"><img src="/research/tcb-chi2021-figure.jpg" alt="Thermoformed circuit boards: fabricated freeform circuits and functional electronic objects" loading="lazy"/><div><h3>Thermoformed Circuit Boards</h3><p>Heat-bent, copper-plated circuits in freeform objects, including interactive lamps and sensors.</p><div class="fabrication-entry-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3411764.3445469">Paper ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/FreddieHong19/Thermoformed-Circuit-Board">Code and fabrication files ↗</a></div></div></article>
  <article class="fabrication-fabrication-entry"><img src="/research/vacuum-formed-sncs2022-figure.png" alt="Vacuum-formed electronics: design of conductive traces, fabrication process and interactive demonstration" loading="lazy"/><div><h3>Vacuum-formed electronics</h3><p>Thin, rigid interactive surfaces with embedded conductive traces, formed from printed sheets.</p><div class="fabrication-entry-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s42979-022-01174-1">Paper ↗</a></div></div></article>
</div></section>
 <section class="strand-strand" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading"><div class="strand-strand-intro"><span>05 / RESEARCH AREA</span><h2 id="privacy-heading">Towards private and trustworthy sensing</h2><p>Sensing systems can reveal considerably more about people than the information they are intended to collect. We investigate methods for limiting unnecessary disclosure while preserving the utility of the data and the services that depend on it.</p><p>Our work on <strong>paralinguistic privacy</strong> explores how sensitive attributes can be filtered from speech signals, including through configurable processing and privacy-preserving computation at the edge.</p></div><div class="directory-privacy-list">
  <article class="planning-paper"><span class="feature-item-index">ACM TRANSACTIONS ON PRIVACY AND SECURITY · 2023</span><h3>Paralinguistic privacy protection at the edge</h3><p>EDGY filters sensitive attributes from voice representations on resource-constrained devices before cloud processing.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3570161">Paper ↗</a> <a href="https://github.com/RanyaJumah/EDGY">Code ↗</a></div></article>
  <article class="planning-paper"><span class="feature-item-index">ACM CCSW · 2020</span><h3>Privacy-preserving voice analysis</h3><p>Disentangled representations help separate useful linguistic information from sensitive paralinguistic attributes.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3411495.3421355">Paper ↗</a> <a href="https://github.com/RanyaJumah/EDGY">Code ↗</a></div></article>
  <article class="planning-paper"><span class="feature-item-index">INTERSPEECH · 2021</span><h3>Configurable privacy-preserving speech recognition</h3><p>Configurable protection of sensitive information in automatic speech-recognition workflows.</p><div class="feature-inline-links"><a href="https://www.isca-archive.org/interspeech_2021/aloufi21_interspeech.pdf">Paper · PDF ↗</a> <a href="https://github.com/RanyaJumah/EDGY">Code ↗</a></div></article>
 </div></section>
</main>
</Base>
